            'safeguarding' => array(
                'title' => 'Safeguarding and child protection',
                'content' => '<section><h2>Our safeguarding commitment</h2><p>The Learning Net aims to provide a safe, respectful online learning environment. Everyone working with children is expected to act in the child\'s best interests, recognise concerns and report them promptly.</p><div class="safeguard-banner"><h3>Designated safeguarding contact</h3><p>Email <a href="mailto:info@thelearningnet.org?subject=Safeguarding%20concern">info@thelearningnet.org</a>. If a child is in immediate danger, contact the emergency services or the appropriate local safeguarding authority.</p></div></section><section><h2>Safer recruitment and DBS</h2><ul class="list"><li>Identity, qualifications and employment history are checked before tutoring work begins</li><li>Tutors working with children are expected to hold the appropriate enhanced DBS or equivalent background check for their role and location</li><li>References, suitability and safeguarding expectations are reviewed</li><li>Safeguarding responsibilities continue through supervision, review and professional conduct requirements</li></ul></section><section><h2>Safe online lessons</h2><ul class="list"><li>Lessons use approved accounts and agreed platforms</li><li>A parent or guardian should know when and where younger learners are attending</li><li>Students should learn in an appropriate shared or family-aware environment where possible</li><li>Tutors must maintain professional boundaries and use approved communication channels</li><li>Sessions, resources and messages must be suitable for the learner\'s age</li><li>Private contact, gifts, secret-keeping and inappropriate personal relationships are prohibited</li></ul></section><section><h2>Recognising and reporting concerns</h2><p>A safeguarding concern may involve abuse, neglect, exploitation, bullying, inappropriate communication, unsafe behaviour or any change that suggests a child may be at risk. Staff and tutors must record facts accurately, avoid investigating themselves and report the concern promptly to the designated safeguarding contact.</p><p>Information is shared only with people who need it to protect the child. Where required, The Learning Net will refer concerns to the relevant local authority, police or safeguarding agency.</p></section><section><h2>Responding to a disclosure</h2><ol><li><strong>Listen:</strong> Take the child seriously and stay calm.</li><li><strong>Do not promise secrecy:</strong> Explain that the information may need to be shared to keep them safe.</li><li><strong>Record:</strong> Write down the child\'s own words and relevant facts as soon as possible.</li><li><strong>Report:</strong> Contact the designated safeguarding lead without delay.</li><li><strong>Escalate:</strong> If immediate danger exists, contact emergency services or the local safeguarding authority.</li></ol></section><section><h2>Raise a safeguarding concern</h2>[ln_form id="safeguarding"]</section><section><h2>Privacy and review</h2><p>Safeguarding records are stored securely and retained only as required by law and child-protection practice. This policy is reviewed when guidance changes or after a safeguarding incident.</p></section>',
                'action' => 'update',
                'lead' => 'The welfare of children and young people is central to every Learning Net lesson, tutor decision and family conversation.',
            ),
            'copyright' => array(
                'title' => 'Copyright Information',
                'content' => '<nav class="policy-nav" aria-label="Policy pages"><a href="https://thelearningnet.org/terms/">Terms &amp; Conditions</a><a href="https://thelearningnet.org/copyright/">Copyright</a><a href="https://thelearningnet.org/disclaimer/">Disclaimer</a><a href="https://thelearningnet.org/cookies/">Cookies</a><a href="https://thelearningnet.org/terms-of-service/">Terms of Services</a><a href="https://thelearningnet.org/data-protection/">Data Protection</a><a href="https://thelearningnet.org/privacy/">Privacy</a><a href="https://thelearningnet.org/safeguarding/">Safeguarding</a></nav><section><h2>Copyright notice</h2><p>© The Learning Net. All rights reserved.</p><p>The content, design, text, graphics, images, videos, logos and all other materials on www.thelearningnet.org, www.thelearningnet.uk and www.thelearningnet.co.uk are the property of Noor 367 Ltd, trading as The Learning Net, or are used with permission from third-party licensors.</p></section><section><h2>Restrictions on use</h2><ul class="list"><li>Do not copy, reproduce, distribute, modify or create derivative works without written authorisation</li><li>Do not use our materials for commercial purposes</li><li>Do not publish or display our content on other websites or platforms without proper attribution</li></ul></section><section><h2>Fair use and educational purposes</h2><p>You may use content for personal, non-commercial educational purposes provided you do not alter or misrepresent it, you credit The Learning Net as the original source and you do not share or distribute it for profit.</p></section><section><h2>Reporting copyright infringement</h2><p>If you believe website content infringes your copyright, email <a href="mailto:info@thelearningnet.org">info@thelearningnet.org</a>.</p></section>',
                'action' => 'update',
                'lead' => 'Copyright and permitted use of Learning Net website and teaching materials.',
            ),
            'disclaimer' => array(
                'title' => 'Disclaimer',
                'content' => '<nav class="policy-nav" aria-label="Policy pages"><a href="https://thelearningnet.org/terms/">Terms &amp; Conditions</a><a href="https://thelearningnet.org/copyright/">Copyright</a><a href="https://thelearningnet.org/disclaimer/">Disclaimer</a><a href="https://thelearningnet.org/cookies/">Cookies</a><a href="https://thelearningnet.org/terms-of-service/">Terms of Services</a><a href="https://thelearningnet.org/data-protection/">Data Protection</a><a href="https://thelearningnet.org/privacy/">Privacy</a><a href="https://thelearningnet.org/safeguarding/">Safeguarding</a></nav><section><h2>1. Educational purpose only</h2><p>The Learning Net provides online tutoring, homeschooling support and educational resources. We do not guarantee specific academic results or exam success. Outcomes depend on individual effort, participation and external factors.</p></section><section><h2>2. No professional advice</h2><p>Website content, articles, resources and tutoring do not constitute legal, financial, medical or psychological advice. Seek an appropriately qualified professional when needed.</p></section><section><h2>3. Accuracy and updates</h2><p>We aim to provide accurate, current information but do not guarantee that all content is error-free, complete or current. Content may be modified without notice.</p></section><section><h2>4. Third-party links and services</h2><p>External links are provided for convenience and do not imply endorsement. We are not responsible for third-party content, privacy policies or practices.</p></section><section><h2>5. Limitation of liability</h2><p>To the fullest extent permitted by law, The Learning Net and its affiliates, directors, employees and tutors are not liable for direct, indirect, incidental or consequential loss arising from website or service use, including data loss, technical failure, downtime or third-party conduct.</p></section><section><h2>6. User responsibility</h2><ul class="list"><li>Verify information before relying on it</li><li>Recognise that academic success depends on effort and participation</li><li>Use the website and services at your own risk</li></ul></section><section><h2>7. Changes</h2><p>This disclaimer may be updated. Continued website use constitutes acceptance of revised terms.</p></section><section><h2>8. Contact</h2><p>Email <a href="mailto:info@thelearningnet.org">info@thelearningnet.org</a>.</p></section>',
                'action' => 'update',
                'lead' => 'Important limits on educational information, results and third-party services.',
            ),
            'cookies' => array(
                'title' => 'Cookies Policy',
                'content' => '<nav class="policy-nav" aria-label="Policy pages"><a href="https://thelearningnet.org/terms/">Terms &amp; Conditions</a><a href="https://thelearningnet.org/copyright/">Copyright</a><a href="https://thelearningnet.org/disclaimer/">Disclaimer</a><a href="https://thelearningnet.org/cookies/">Cookies</a><a href="https://thelearningnet.org/terms-of-service/">Terms of Services</a><a href="https://thelearningnet.org/data-protection/">Data Protection</a><a href="https://thelearningnet.org/privacy/">Privacy</a><a href="https://thelearningnet.org/safeguarding/">Safeguarding</a></nav><section><h2>1. What are cookies?</h2><p>Cookies are small text files stored on a computer, tablet or phone. They can remember preferences, enable website functions and support analytics.</p></section><section><h2>2. Types of cookies we use</h2><h3>Essential cookies</h3><p>Session and security cookies help the website operate and protect against fraud. The legal basis is legitimate interest.</p><h3>Performance and analytics cookies</h3><p>These collect anonymous usage information. Services such as Google Analytics may be used with consent.</p><h3>Functionality cookies</h3><p>These remember preferences such as language or login choices and may be disabled in settings.</p><h3>Advertising and third-party cookies</h3><p>With consent, Google Ads or Facebook Pixel may measure activity for relevant advertising.</p></section><section><h2>3. Consent</h2><p>A cookie banner may offer choices to accept all cookies, manage preferences or reject non-essential cookies.</p></section><section><h2>4. Managing cookies</h2><p>Browser privacy settings can remove or block cookies. Blocking essential cookies may affect website operation.</p></section><section><h2>5. Third-party services</h2><p>Google Analytics, Facebook Pixel, Stripe and PayPal may process data, including outside the UK and EEA, with protections intended to support UK GDPR compliance.</p></section><section><h2>6. Changes</h2><p>This policy may be updated and changes will be posted on the website.</p></section><section><h2>7. Contact</h2><p>Email <a href="mailto:info@thelearningnet.org">info@thelearningnet.org</a> with questions about cookies.</p></section>',
                'action' => 'update',
                'lead' => 'How cookies and similar technologies are described across The Learning Net websites.',
            ),
            'terms-of-service' => array(
                'title' => 'Terms of Services',
                'content' => '<nav class="policy-nav" aria-label="Policy pages"><a href="https://thelearningnet.org/terms/">Terms &amp; Conditions</a><a href="https://thelearningnet.org/copyright/">Copyright</a><a href="https://thelearningnet.org/disclaimer/">Disclaimer</a><a href="https://thelearningnet.org/cookies/">Cookies</a><a href="https://thelearningnet.org/terms-of-service/">Terms of Services</a><a href="https://thelearningnet.org/data-protection/">Data Protection</a><a href="https://thelearningnet.org/privacy/">Privacy</a><a href="https://thelearningnet.org/safeguarding/">Safeguarding</a></nav><section><h2>1. About us</h2><p>The Learning Net is the trading name of Noor 367 Ltd, a company registered in England and Wales under company number 12495289.</p></section><section><h2>2. Our services</h2><p>We provide online tutoring, homeschooling support and educational resources from Key Stage 2 to IGCSE and A-Level, delivered through virtual learning sessions.</p></section><section><h2>3. Eligibility</h2><ul class="list"><li>Users must be at least 16 or have parental or guardian consent</li><li>Account information must be accurate</li><li>The website must be used for educational purposes only</li></ul></section><section><h2>4. Accounts and security</h2><ul class="list"><li>Keep login details confidential</li><li>You are responsible for activity under your account</li><li>Report suspected unauthorised access immediately</li></ul></section><section><h2>5. Payment and refunds</h2><h3>Fees and payments</h3><p>Fees are confirmed before payment. Payment through an approved method must be completed before booking confirmation.</p><h3>Cancellations and refunds</h3><p>A booked session may be cancelled with at least 24 hours\' notice for a full refund. Cancellations with less notice are non-refundable. If a tutor cancels, the lesson will be refunded or rescheduled.</p></section><section><h2>6. Tutor responsibilities</h2><p>Tutors are independent contractors rather than employees. Background checks are conducted, but specific tutoring results are not guaranteed.</p></section><section><h2>7. Student responsibilities</h2><p>Students must arrive on time and behave respectfully. Disruptive behaviour may result in suspension or termination.</p></section><section><h2>8. Intellectual property</h2><p>Courses, content and materials are owned by Noor 367 Ltd or licensed from third parties and may not be copied, distributed or sold without permission.</p></section><section><h2>9. Prohibited activities</h2><ul class="list"><li>Sharing offensive, abusive or illegal content</li><li>Attempting to hack, disrupt or exploit the website</li><li>Impersonating another person or misrepresenting identity</li></ul></section><section><h2>10. Limitation of liability</h2><p>We do not guarantee exam results or academic performance and are not liable for indirect, incidental or consequential losses to the fullest extent permitted by law.</p></section><section><h2>11. Data protection</h2><p>Personal data is handled under our Privacy Policy and UK GDPR responsibilities.</p></section><section><h2>12. Third-party websites</h2><p>Third-party links are governed by their own policies and are not controlled or endorsed by The Learning Net.</p></section><section><h2>13. Suspension or termination</h2><p>Accounts may be suspended or terminated for non-payment, inappropriate behaviour or intellectual-property breaches.</p></section><section><h2>14. Changes</h2><p>Continued use after terms are updated constitutes acceptance.</p></section><section><h2>15. Governing law and disputes</h2><p>English law applies. Disputes should be addressed through negotiation or mediation before legal action.</p></section><section><h2>16. Contact</h2><p>Email <a href="mailto:info@thelearningnet.org">info@thelearningnet.org</a>.</p></section>',
                'action' => 'update',
                'lead' => 'The service rules for students, parents, tutors and website users.',
            ),
            'data-protection' => array(
                'title' => 'Data Protection Policy',
                'content' => '<nav class="policy-nav" aria-label="Policy pages"><a href="https://thelearningnet.org/terms/">Terms &amp; Conditions</a><a href="https://thelearningnet.org/copyright/">Copyright</a><a href="https://thelearningnet.org/disclaimer/">Disclaimer</a><a href="https://thelearningnet.org/cookies/">Cookies</a><a href="https://thelearningnet.org/terms-of-service/">Terms of Services</a><a href="https://thelearningnet.org/data-protection/">Data Protection</a><a href="https://thelearningnet.org/privacy/">Privacy</a><a href="https://thelearningnet.org/safeguarding/">Safeguarding</a></nav><section><h2>1. Introduction</h2><p>The Learning Net, trading under Noor 367 Ltd, is committed to protecting personal data in line with the UK General Data Protection Regulation and Data Protection Act 2018 across www.thelearningnet.org, www.thelearningnet.uk and www.thelearningnet.co.uk.</p></section><section><h2>2. Who we are</h2><p><strong>Company:</strong> Noor 367 Ltd<br><strong>Trading name:</strong> The Learning Net<br><strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:info@thelearningnet.org">info@thelearningnet.org</a></p></section><section><h2>3. Personal data we collect</h2><h3>Students and parents</h3><ul class="list"><li>Name, age and contact details</li><li>Parent or guardian details for under-16s</li><li>Payment details processed by third parties</li><li>Learning history, progress reports and session recordings</li><li>Communications with tutors</li></ul><h3>Tutors and staff</h3><ul class="list"><li>Name, qualifications and employment history</li><li>Enhanced DBS checks</li><li>Bank details for payment processing</li></ul><h3>Website users</h3><ul class="list"><li>IP address and device or browser information</li><li>Cookies and tracking data described in our Cookies Policy</li></ul></section><section><h2>4. How we use data</h2><ul class="list"><li>Deliver tutoring, scheduling, progress tracking and service communications</li><li>Process payments securely</li><li>Meet safeguarding and child-protection obligations</li><li>Improve the website and services</li><li>Send reminders and updates</li></ul></section><section><h2>Lawful bases</h2><p>We rely on contractual obligation, legitimate interests, legal compliance and consent according to the processing purpose.</p></section><section><h2>5. Storage, security and retention</h2><p>Safeguards include encryption, secure UK/EU servers and access controls. Student records are described as retained for three years after last use, tutor records for six years after termination, communications for 12 months unless legally required, and payment data is handled by payment processors rather than stored by us.</p></section><section><h2>6. Sharing personal data</h2><p>We do not sell or rent personal data. Information may be shared with tutors for lesson delivery, payment providers such as Stripe or PayPal, and authorities where legally required for safeguarding or fraud prevention.</p></section><section><h2>7. Your UK GDPR rights</h2><ul class="list"><li>Access your data</li><li>Correct inaccurate information</li><li>Request erasure</li><li>Restrict processing</li><li>Object to marketing processing</li><li>Withdraw consent where consent is the basis</li></ul></section><section><h2>8. Children\'s data and safeguarding</h2><p>Parental or guardian consent is required for students under 16. Child-protection procedures are followed in line with UK safeguarding requirements.</p></section><section><h2>9. International transfers</h2><p>Data is described as stored within the UK and EEA. Where transfers go elsewhere, UK GDPR safeguards and standard contractual clauses are used.</p></section><section><h2>10. Changes</h2><p>Updates may be posted when legal requirements change, with significant changes communicated by email where appropriate.</p></section><section><h2>11. Contact and complaints</h2><p>Email <a href="mailto:info@thelearningnet.org">info@thelearningnet.org</a> to exercise your rights. We aim to respond within one month. Concerns may also be raised with the UK Information Commissioner\'s Office.</p></section>',
                'action' => 'update',
                'lead' => 'How Noor 367 Ltd collects, uses, stores and protects personal information.',
