                'title' => 'Empowering Students Through Leadership',
                'date' => '2 March 2023',
                'content' => '<section><h2>Understanding the IGCSE exam format</h2><p>IGCSE exams are a crucial milestone. Strong preparation begins by understanding how each subject is assessed. Papers may include multiple-choice questions, structured written responses, data analysis, case studies and practical assessments.</p><p>Check the syllabus, number of papers, weighting and question types before planning revision.</p></section><section><h2>Best IGCSE revision resources</h2><p>Useful resources include textbooks, online courses, interactive apps and dedicated revision websites. The Learning Net supports students with IGCSE and O Level textbooks, workbooks, revision notes, video tutorials, quizzes and guided lessons.</p><ul class="list"><li>Gojimo for quick subject quizzes</li><li>Quizlet for customisable flashcards</li><li>Brainscape for spaced flashcard practice</li></ul></section><section><h2>Use past papers effectively</h2><ol><li><strong>Simulate exam conditions:</strong> Complete papers under timed conditions.</li><li><strong>Review mark schemes:</strong> Study how marks are awarded.</li><li><strong>Identify weak areas:</strong> Return to topics where marks were lost.</li><li><strong>Practise regularly:</strong> Use several papers to build confidence and familiarity.</li></ol></section><section><h2>Proven study techniques</h2><h3>Active recall and mind maps</h3><ul class="list"><li>Use flashcards to retrieve key ideas</li><li>Create mind maps to connect related topics</li></ul><h3>Group study and discussion</h3><p>Explain difficult ideas to peers; teaching someone else can expose gaps and strengthen understanding.</p><h3>Exam strategy</h3><ul class="list"><li>Allocate time according to the marks available</li><li>Use relevant real-world examples where appropriate</li><li>Respond directly to command words such as explain, evaluate and compare</li></ul></section><section><h2>Additional support</h2><p>If a topic continues to feel difficult, one-to-one tuition can provide precise explanations, guided practice and feedback.</p></section><section><h2>Final thoughts</h2><p>Successful IGCSE revision combines a clear plan, consistent practice and resources matched to the exact specification. Stay committed, review mistakes and build confidence one topic at a time.</p></section>',
